    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But pausing doesn't change anything. The silence is still here. The emptiness is still here. It's not a pause, it's just... lingering. If the story is over, why keep the characters on stage? It feels like the only way to truly find peace, to actually finish what was started, is to embrace the end. The steel is so cold, but it feels honest. It doesn't promise new chapters or empty hope. It just offers a way to make the weight finally stop.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
